# golgi — the cell's router, with no router in it
#
# The Golgi is sold as a sorting office: a protein arrives wearing a header, a
# clerk reads the header, the protein is sent to the right door. That picture
# has a little man in it. Take him out.
#
# What is actually there is a CONVEYOR and three LEAKS. Cargo arrives from the
# ER at the cis face, matures along the stack (cis → medial → trans) — one
# directional flow, the cisternae handing cargo forward — and piles up at the
# trans face, the shipping dock. From the dock there are three exits running in
# parallel: to the lysosome, to the plasma membrane, to secretion. Each exit has
# its own RATE. A "tag" (mannose-6-phosphate for the lysosome, a signal for
# secretion, default for the membrane) is nothing more than which exit a given
# protein is FAST down. No clerk reads anything. The split between the three
# destinations is just the ratio of the three rate constants — competition, not
# decision. That is the same move café and gene-express make: behaviour that
# looks chosen falls out of rates that merely compete.
#
# Watch it run: the three destination buckets fill to steady heights in the
# ratio 0.15 : 0.40 : 0.25 — the routing table, drawn by the math, not asserted.
# Change one exit's k and the whole distribution re-balances. That IS retargeting
# a protein: you don't re-educate a clerk, you change a rate.
#
# THE GAP THIS EXPOSES (the next model's job): Strombild splits a FLUX, not an
# item. It says "40% of the trans pool leaves toward the membrane per unit time,"
# never "THIS protein, bearing THIS header, goes to the membrane." For a flux,
# competing rates is the honest and complete story. The day a model needs to
# follow one tagged item through a branch — to say the header is read once and
# commits — that is the gap, and it wants a token/identity the stocks don't have.

node cis        : range(0, 30), init(0)  @ bucket(fill = dots)        # cargo arriving, untagged
node trans      : range(0, 30), init(0)   @ bucket(fill = dots)       # the shipping dock (tagged, sorted by rate)
node lysosome   : range(0, 20), init(0) @ bucket(fill = dots)             # exit 1 — mannose-6-phosphate
node membrane   : range(0, 20), init(0) @ bucket(fill = dots)             # exit 2 — default / cell surface
node secretion  : range(0, 20), init(0) @ bucket(fill = dots)            # exit 3 — secretion signal
external er          # the source: protein folded and shipped out of the ER
external void        # destinations turn over (proteins are used / degraded)

er    -> cis        : constant(c = 6)                  # steady supply from the ER
cis   -> trans      : proportional(k = 0.6)            # maturation: the stack hands cargo forward

# the three exits — same pool, three competing rates. the k's ARE the tags.
trans -> lysosome   : proportional(of = trans, k = 0.15)
trans -> membrane   : proportional(of = trans, k = 0.40)
trans -> secretion  : proportional(of = trans, k = 0.25)

# each destination turns over, so its steady height reads its routing rate
lysosome  -> void   : proportional(k = 0.2)
membrane  -> void   : proportional(k = 0.2)
secretion -> void   : proportional(k = 0.2)

pathway route : er->cis, cis->trans, trans->lysosome, trans->membrane, trans->secretion, lysosome->void, membrane->void, secretion->void
